e1000: disable EEE on a CE4100 PHY attached through phylib

The MAC has no LPI support, but phylib keeps the PHY's default EEE
advertisement. With EEE negotiated, an RTL8211E blinks its link LED
about once a second while the link idles, so a link LED offloaded to
the PHY does not show the link state. Tell phylib the MAC has no EEE.

Author: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000/e1000_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000/e1000_main.c
index 00e8813..f3b21c2 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000/e1000_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000/e1000_main.c
@@ -1088,6 +1088,8 @@ static int e1000_connect_phy(struct e1000_adapter *adapter)
 		err = -ENODEV;
 		goto out;
 	}
+	/* The MAC has no LPI support */
+	phy_disable_eee(phydev);
 
 	hw->fixed_link = true;
 	hw->fixed_link_speed = SPEED_1000;
